LOGBOOK.md:398:- FIX: one board edge — `link(TASK-260715-29ws8l, blocked_by=TASK-260715-ypo7yo)`, cycle-checked over the whole graph first. It orders all three because 29ws8l already blocks the other two, and it is semantically real: 29ws8l **AC2** specifies "App Group and `providerConfiguration` data" and **AC4** specifies "Keychain accessibility, access group" — exactly what rules G4 and K2 decide. Authoring it without this matrix reproduces the iOS-only assumption OC-1 was raised against.
