LOGBOOK.md:1264:- REVIEW FINDING: The same revision has a recorded real `swift test` failure in `HarnessTests.cancellationCleanup` (`TimedOut()` at line 140), while the test still uses a scheduler-count loop of 10,000 `Task.yield()` calls. The new clean matrix, coverage run, and 50 targeted repeats passed, but they do not invalidate the observed nondeterministic failure or prove the unchanged race is eliminated.
LOGBOOK.md:1298:- FIX: Bundle validation now owns one no-follow directory descriptor, opens manifest/assets relative to it with `O_NOFOLLOW`, checks `fstat` size limits before allocation, caps manifest JSON at 64 KiB and assets at 16 MiB, and streams exact-size SHA-256/header/build-identity validation.
LOGBOOK.md:1303:- FIX: Initial bundle publication now uses parent-descriptor-anchored Darwin `renameatx_np(RENAME_EXCL)` or Linux `renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE)`, so a destination created after the absence check is preserved and publication fails closed. Existing stale-directory replacement remains an atomic exchange with ownership-aware cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md:1304:- FIX: The accepted gzip/USTAR archive is opened once with `O_NOFOLLOW`, bounded by `fstat` before reading, streamed for SHA-256, rewound, and parsed through that same owned file object. Parsing accepts only the exact four canonical regular members and bounded zero trailer, avoiding unbounded tar metadata materialization. File-object conversion failures now close every still-owned descriptor, and output permissions use `fchmod` on the owned descriptor.
LOGBOOK.md:1309:- FIX: `generate_bundle` now carries the initial destination-existed state into publication. An initially absent destination uses parent-descriptor-anchored atomic no-replace for the entire attempt, regardless of any later path appearance, so a raced foreign inode and marker survive while owned staging is cleaned.
LOGBOOK.md:1314:- FIX: The frozen publication state now carries A's `(st_dev, st_ino)`. Existing-bundle validation uses a parent-anchored no-follow descriptor whose `fstat` identity must match A; publication requires the same identity immediately before exchange, verifies the displaced identity afterward, and atomically rolls back a last-window mismatch before owned-staging cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md:1319:- FIX: Cleanup now reuses the publication parent descriptor, opens the displaced directory relative to it with no-follow semantics, verifies the opened `(st_dev, st_ino)`, and removes only the bounded flat relay bundle entries through that owned descriptor. It rechecks the top-level identity before parent-relative `rmdir`; unsupported names and non-regular entries fail closed.
LOGBOOK.md:1359:- FIX: `MacOSSystemKeychainHandle` now has an inert internal fixture identity accepted only by injected fake Security clients; the live client rejects fixture handles before its injectable matcher, and a spy proves zero `SecItemCopyMatching` reachability. The suite no longer calls any live Security API and asserts one exact scoped reference query, no enumeration/fallback, malformed-reference zero calls, cancellation cleanup, passphrase states, and 16 bounded secret-lifecycle repetitions.
