@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# TASK-260715-135rr8 — Physical Mac memory, lifecycle, and concurrency matrix
+
+Status: ready for review
+
+## Outcome
+
+The bounded physical-Mac HEV/bridge baseline met the provisional incremental
+25–30 MiB target through the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling. The
+500-session incremental physical footprint was 11,976,704 B. This leaves
+19,480,576 B inside a 30 MiB envelope, but it is not a whole-extension budget:
+SSH, DNS, relay, caches, and reconnect overlap remain unmeasured and must fit
+inside that remainder before the target can be accepted for production.
+
+| Stage | Live sessions | Footprint | Peak | Descriptors | Threads | Drops |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 100 | 100 | 12,354,160 B | 12,354,160 B | 211 | 10 | 0 |
+| 250 | 250 | 15,270,512 B | 15,270,512 B | 511 | 10 | 0 |
+| Measured ceiling | 500 | 20,038,256 B | 20,054,640 B | 1,010 | 10 | 0 |
+
+The run stopped at the configured 500-session ceiling. It did not force the
+upstream 1,200 value. Cleanup returned descriptors from 1,010 to 3 and process
+threads from 10 to 9.
+
+## Lifecycle and fault evidence
+
+- 100 real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles passed with no monotonic footprint
+  growth and exact restoration of owned descriptors, sessions, queued batches,
+  outstanding reads, boundary ownership, and close stages.
+- Seven startup cancellation stages and seven cleanup cancellation stages
+  passed through `PacketFlowBridge.start` and ordered teardown.
+- Fifty host-termination iterations returned shell exit 143 and cleaned every
+  harness-owned resource.
+- Mixed bidirectional IPv4/IPv6 TCP traffic, half-close, reset, UDP-in-TCP, and
+  a real stalled-path pressure run passed.
+- Negative production-entry evidence: `PacketFlowBridge.start` rejects
+  `maximumSessionCount=0` as `descriptorBorrowFailure` before HEV starts.
+
+## Availability and deferred gaps
+
+- `os_proc_available_memory`: unavailable. The public SDK explicitly marks it
+  unavailable on macOS; no host-memory proxy was substituted.
+- HEV queued bytes: unknown because the pinned runtime exposes no queue-byte
+  gauge. Configured task stack (24,576 B), TCP buffer (4,096 B), bridge socket
+  buffer (16,384 B), sessions, traffic counters, and drops are recorded.
+- Process-wide Swift task count: unavailable; process threads are recorded as a
+  distinct metric and not used as a proxy.
+- Soft/pressure/critical ordering: deferred until SSH admission integration.
+  The current pressure source is advisory and has no production policy
+  consumer. Real bounded socket pressure and critical bridge teardown pass.
+- Physical iPhone is deferred with iOS. Sleep/wake is deferred because a
+  headless bounded run cannot change global host power state.
+- No NetworkExtension, VPN, route, DNS, interface, packet filter, SSH session,
+  Keychain, sudo, `powermetrics`, `memory_pressure`, or global setting was used.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Physical matrix: 1/1 passed, exit 0.
+- 100-cycle real HEV lifecycle: 1/1 passed, exit 0.
+- Startup/cleanup cancellation matrix: 8 tests including 23 parameterized
+  cases passed, exit 0.
+- Host termination: 50/50 passed, exit 0.
+- Full suite: 480 tests in 40 suites passed, exit 0; 25 declared known
+  ReluxNIOSSH-adapter-unavailable issues remain unchanged.
+- Full coverage suite: 480 tests passed, exit 0.
+- Affected coverage: 84.84% regions, 96.02% functions, 93.09% lines.
+- Strict Swift format lint: exit 0.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+```bash
+RELUX_RUN_PHYSICAL_MEMORY_MATRIX=1 swift test \
+  --filter HEVIntegrationTests.physicalMemoryAndConcurrencyMatrix
+swift test --filter HEVIntegrationTests.realHEVHundredLifecycleCycles
+swift test --filter PacketFlowBridgeLifecycleTests
+swift test --filter HarnessTests.cancellationCleanup
+swift test --enable-code-coverage --skip-build
+```
+
+Raw report:
+`.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/TASK-260715-135rr8_raw-memory-matrix.json`
+
+Primary logs:
+
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-physical-matrix-02.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-lifecycle-100-01.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-cancellation-lifecycle-01.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-host-termination-01.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-full-01.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-full-coverage-01.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/llvm-cov-affected-02.log`
+- `.temp/TASK-260715-135rr8/swift-format-lint-02.log`
+
+## Anomalies encountered
+
+Initial batch probes conflated bridge socket pressure with HEV admission and
+were retained as failing logs. Sequential admission isolated the safe 500-flow
+row. A first `proc_pid_rusage` Swift-importer attempt aborted the opt-in test;
+the final sampler uses public `task_info(TASK_VM_INFO)` and passed. These failed
+attempts are not counted as passing gates.
